# deploy/env/.env.example — TEMPLATE (placeholder values only, NO real secrets).
#
# The Feishu code-review event server (event_server.py --mode ws) needs these in
# its environment to authenticate and operate. The REAL values live in the
# PERSISTENT (container/volume-mounted) file:
#
#   /var/lib/report-server/daily/cr-env/env.sh
#
# That file is bind-mounted into the agent container at the same path and is
# read by the watchdog (/startup.sh). It is NOT in git.
#
# -------- How to (re)generate the real persisted env.sh ----------
# Capture it from a currently-working bot process (exact NUL-separated environ):
#
#   BOTPID=$(docker exec chaos-agent-cr bash -c \
#     "pgrep -f 'event_server.py --mode ws' | head -1")
#   docker exec chaos-agent-cr bash -c \
#     "cat > /var/lib/report-server/daily/cr-env/env.sh" < /proc/$BOTPID/environ
#   # (on the host, use /proc/<host-pid>/environ + docker exec -i redirection)
#
# Or start with this template and fill real values, then run deploy/apply.sh.
#
# -------- Variables ------------------------------------------------
# Feishu long-connection app credentials (open.feishu.cn app):
FEISHU_APP_ID=
FEISHU_APP_SECRET=
# The topic group the bot replies in (leave empty if config resolves it):
FEISHU_CHAT_ID=
# Webhook for health/alert notifications (Feishu bot webhook):
FEISHU_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Claude/Anthropic-compatible LLM API for reviews + interact:
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# Jira / GitLab credentials (needed to resolve + clone review branches):
JIRA_HOST=
JIRA_TOKEN=
GITLAB_USER=
GITLAB_TOKEN=
CR_GITLAB_USER=
CR_GITLAB_TOKEN=
# Jenkins (inherited; informational):
JENKINS_URL=
JENKINS_MASTER_URL=
JENKINS_AGENT_NAME=
#
# NOTE: keep JSON keys in sync with the running bot's environment. The safest
# baseline is to copy the live bot's environ (method above), not this template.
